{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Intrinsic Limit of Law.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Intrinsic Limit of Law.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"intrinsic limit of law intrinsic limit of law","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Intrinsic Limit of Law.md","fileName":"Intrinsic Limit of Law.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Intrinsic Limit of Law","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-17 09:48\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Privacy Theory and Legal Limits]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Privacy Theory and Legal Limits","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Intrinsic Limit of Law.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Intrinsic Limit of Law.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"intrinsic limit of law intrinsic limit of law","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Intrinsic Limit of Law.md","fileName":"Intrinsic Limit of Law.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Intrinsic Limit of Law","heading":"Intrinsic Limit of Law","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An intrinsic limit of law is a boundary that follows from the conditions under which a legal order can govern persons, rather than from a discretionary policy choice. The source argues that privacy can function as such a limit in an age of extensive data collection.\n\nIf law reaches every aspect of thought and conduct, the autonomy required to form intentions and direct a life is weakened. The limit protects a domain in which people can exist as agents subject to law rather than merely as objects of observation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Privacy Theory and Legal Limits","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Intrinsic Limit of Law.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Intrinsic Limit of Law.md","sourceType":"markdown","